aria in African children</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>332</volume><fpage>1399</fpage><lpage>1404</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7723795</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pctr-0020002-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>English</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Waruiru</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Amukoye</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawley</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Deep breathing in children with severe malaria: Indicator of metabolic acidosis and poor outcome</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>521</fpage><lpage>524</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8940984</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pctr-0020002-b013"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maitland</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pamba</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Newton</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Response to volume resuscitation in children with severe malaria</article-title><source>Pediatr Crit Care Med</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>426</fpage><lpage>431</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14525636</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pctr-0020002-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maitland</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pamba</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>English</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Peshu</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>K<